const HERO_PROSE="Friends, Romans, countrymen, lend me your ears; I come to bury Caesar, not to praise him. The evil that men do lives after them; the good is oft interred with their bones; so let it be with Caesar. Here, under leave of Brutus and the rest, come I to speak in Caesar's funeral. He was my friend, faithful and just to me. "
